  ],
  "mach:judgement": "Adopt",
  "mach:judgementReason": "One of the most widely cited medical image segmentation tools in research — 8,000+ academic paper citations, 20+ years of continuous development, funded by NIH/NLM. GPL-3.0, v4.4.0 (August 2025), 431 stars. Part of the ITK ecosystem: ITK provides the segmentation algorithms; ITK-SNAP provides an interactive desktop application for manual and semi-automatic segmentation workflows in research and pre-clinical settings.",
